From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 11:15:08 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 41/41] net: ethernet: mtk_eth_soc: do not save uninitialized
 TDMA state

An early hang exit jumps to the out label before the TDMA reads. The
out label then saves uninitialized cur_fsm and ipq10 values. Start
with the saved values, so an early exit keeps them.

Signed-off-by: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
index b1aa172da45a..bdbdda9e78b0 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
@@ -4385,7 +4385,9 @@ static bool mtk_hw_check_dma_hang(struct mtk_eth *eth)
 	bool oq_hang, cdm1_busy, adma_busy;
 	bool wtx_busy, cdm_full, oq_free;
 	u32 wdidx, val, gdm1_fc, gdm2_fc, gdm3_fc;
-	u32 tdma_glo_cfg, cur_fsm, ipq10;
+	u32 tdma_glo_cfg;
+	/* An early hang exit skips the TDMA reads: keep the saved values */
+	u32 cur_fsm = eth->reset.pre_fsm, ipq10 = eth->reset.pre_ipq10;
 	bool rx_busy, tx_busy, cur_fsm_tx, cur_fsm_rx;
 
 	bool qfsm_hang, qfwd_hang;
